*AI RECOMMENDATION LOGIC*
Movie Recommendation System
A handful of code lines spark a tool shaped around film tastes. When someone picks preferred categories, suggestions appear through quiet logic. Built with Python, it listens then offers titles tied to chosen moods. Favorite types guide what shows up next. No buttons scream. It just matches patterns without fuss.
📌 Features
- Accepts multiple genres as input.
- Matches user preferences with movie genres.
- Calculates a match score for each movie.
Relevance decides the order of suggestions. What shows up first matches your needs most closely - other options follow behind. Matching strength shapes the list from top to bottom.
Match ratings show up alongside movie picks you might like. A number tells how close each film fits what you enjoy watching.

How It Works

1. A comma marks each genre someone picks. One after another they fill the line. Favorite styles appear just like that. Separated neatly down the list. Each choice shows what they like.
2. A match forms when the typed genres line up with a film’s listed types. Each movie gets checked like that.
3. From time to time, a value shows how many types of stories both sides share. That total becomes the mark used to compare them.
4. When a film shares even one genre, it might show up in suggestions.
5. Match score decides the ranking, highest first.

